 1946 European Champion. Bóbis then met Armstrong for the gold medal, with the Hungarian winning by fall in 9:49."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bóbis did not retire, winning silver in Greco-Roman at the 1950 World Championships. Antonsson would repeat as silver medalist in " [:a {:href "/results/123428"} "this class in 1952"] " and also competed at the " [:a {:href "/results/124182"} "1956"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/124528"} "1960 Olympics"] ", with less success. He won the 1949 European and 1951 World Championships in this class. Armstrong would win the 1950 British Empire Games title in this class, and he also played cricket for Australia in an Ashes’ Test match against Great Britain in 1946."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "146"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58549"} "Gyula Bóbis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "262"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60009"} "Bertil Antonsson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "140"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/57143"} "Jim Armstrong"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td